{
  "dom_id": "step-q159875",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Suppose ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{11}$ is an I.I.D random sample with ${X}_{i}∼\\text{Exp}(\\theta )$ and unknown rate parameter $\\theta .$ For a particular sample ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{11},$ you're given that \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{11}{x}_{i}=8.8.\n$$\n\nFind the likelihood function of the sample.\n\n*Hint: The probability density function for an exponential random variable is given by* \n\n$$\nf(x;\\theta )=\\theta {e}^{-\\theta x},\\,x\\ge 0.\n$$",
